From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:50:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sb/intel/lynxpoint: Route all ports to xHCI only before the
 finalize

APM_CNT_ROUTE_ALL_XHCI switches every USB port from the EHCI
controllers to the xHCI one from SMM. Ramstage asks for it at the
init of the xHCI device, before the finalize; after it, the only code
that can write the APMC port is the OS, and nothing in the OS should
move the ports behind the drivers' back. Refuse the command once the
chipset is finalized, as the finalize itself is refused a second time.
Without it the SMI handler is a way for ring 0 to reconfigure a system
resource outside the ACPI methods, which the WSMT table would promise
is not there.

TEST=Not built. On a W541: the ports still route to xHCI at boot
(lsusb -t shows the devices under the xHCI root hubs), and "outb 0xca,
0xb2" from the OS logs the refusal on the console and changes nothing.
---
 src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/smihandler.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/smihandler.c b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/smihandler.c
index fb9ba87b..8e009844 100644
--- a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/smihandler.c
+++ b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/smihandler.c
@@ -368,6 +368,11 @@ static void southbridge_smi_apmc(void)
 		break;
 #if !CONFIG(SOUTHBRIDGE_INTEL_WILDCATPOINT)
 	case APM_CNT_ROUTE_ALL_XHCI:
+		/* Ramstage asks for it at device init; after the finalize only the OS could */
+		if (chipset_finalized) {
+			printk(BIOS_WARNING, "SMI#: xHCI route all refused after the finalize\n");
+			break;
+		}
 		usb_xhci_route_all();
 		break;
 #endif
